index 0000000..adf8fe9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`, both in the recency bookkeeping:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A cache hit returned the value but left the
+   entry's position in the `OrderedDict` unchanged, so a recently-read key could
+   still be evicted as "least recently used". Fixed by calling
+   `self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a successful (non-expired) hit, since both
+   `get` and `put` are documented to count as "use".
+
+2. **`put` evicted before checking for an existing key.** When the cache was at
+   capacity, `put` unconditionally popped the LRU entry first — so merely
+   updating an existing key evicted an unrelated entry. Fixed by only evicting
+   when the key is new (`if key not in self._data and len(...) >= capacity`);
+   updates now happen in place and just move the key to the most-recently-used
+   end.
